"""AS5047U - 14-bit on-axis magnetic rotary position sensor, TSSOP-14, 3.3 V supply mode.

Datasheet: ams AS5047U DS v1-00 (2018-10-30).

Application mode: 3.3 V operation (Figure 11, right). VDD and VDD3V3 are tied to
the 3.0-3.6 V supply (Figure 6, VDD3V3 with VDD = VDD3V3). The 5 V mode, with
1 uF on the internal LDO output, is not supported by this package.

Bare part: the 100 nF from the tied VDD/VDD3V3 node to GND that Figure 11 shows
belongs to the board.

Pins (Figure 4):
- TEST (5) is tied to GND, as required.
- U, V, W/PWM and I/PWM are push-pull outputs, left open (note 5).
- VDD3V3 is typed power_in in the symbol: in 3.3 V mode it is a supply input,
  not the LDO output.
- CSn, CLK and MOSI must not float (note 1). Where the SPI host can release
  them (an MCU in reset), the board adds the pull-up on CSn and pull-downs on
  CLK and MOSI of notes 2 and 3.

Mechanical: the Hall array centre is the package centre, 0.306 mm below the
package top, radius 1.25 mm (Figure 63). Package A2 1.00 mm nominal, A 1.20 mm
max, D 5.00 x E1 4.40 mm, E 6.40 mm, 0.65 mm pitch (Figure 60): JEDEC MO-153
AB-1. Footprint SOP65P640X120-14N (IPC-7351 name for that package) and STEP
from the Micras Altium EncoderLib.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Spi")

VDD = io(Power(voltage="3.0V to 3.6V"))
GND = io(Ground)
SPI = io(Spi)
A = io(Net)
B = io(Net)

Component(
    name="AS5047U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="AS5047U.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("SOP65P640X120-14N.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="AS5047U-HTSM", manufacturer="ams OSRAM"),
    prefix="IC",
    pins={
        "~{CS}": SPI.CS,
        "CLK": SPI.CLK,
        "MISO": SPI.MISO,
        "MOSI": SPI.MOSI,
        "TEST": GND,
        "B": B,
        "A": A,
        "W/PWM": NotConnected(),
        "V": NotConnected(),
        "U": NotConnected(),
        "VDD": VDD,
        "VDD3V3": VDD,
        "GND": GND,
        "I/PWM": NotConnected(),
    },
)
